{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For the sacred.</b> That is, because all the works listed in the portion are not forbidden for an ordinary person to make, except for these two things, which are the anointing oil and the incense of spices — therefore Scripture was precise to say concerning them <b>for the sacred</b>, to say of them that the design of their making is uniquely designated for the sacred, and the sanctity takes effect upon the prescribed measure of the thing by virtue of its designation alone — unlike all other works in the world, where unless one declares it sacred it is not sacred."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:50.604245043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}